WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.457
Welcome to the Mosaic
Practitioner Certification.

00:00:03.457 --> 00:00:08.395
Over this course you'll learn to put
the Mosaic Performance Framework,

00:00:08.395 --> 00:00:09.524
developed by Dr.

00:00:09.524 --> 00:00:12.275
Chris Cancialosi, to work with clients.

00:00:12.275 --> 00:00:16.508
You'll choose the right tool,
run it well, read it honestly,

00:00:16.508 --> 00:00:19.330
and brief the people who will act on it.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.857
This short orientation
takes about twenty minutes.

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:27.927
If you're here, you're going to put
Mosaic tools in front of clients.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:31.561
That means a CEO will read
a culture report you set up.

00:00:31.561 --> 00:00:34.469
A leader will open
feedback from their team.

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:39.425
A nurse will trust that the story they
shared can't be traced back to them.

00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:42.267
This course gets you
ready for all of that.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:47.554
You'll learn the Mosaic Performance
Framework, the model every tool is built on.

00:00:47.554 --> 00:00:51.122
You'll learn the tools
themselves: the Culture Mosaic,

00:00:51.122 --> 00:00:54.823
the Culture Progress Monitor,
the Leadership Mosaic 360,

00:00:54.823 --> 00:00:56.806
Mosaic Signal and Culture Dig.

00:00:56.806 --> 00:01:01.233
You'll learn when to use each one,
how to set it up in SurveyCraft,

00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:03.811
and how to run it from order to report.

00:01:03.811 --> 00:01:06.256
Most of the course is about judgment.

00:01:06.256 --> 00:01:09.032
What's real in the data, and what's noise?

00:01:09.032 --> 00:01:10.882
What can you honestly claim?

00:01:10.882 --> 00:01:16.301
How do you turn a sixty-slide report into
a ten-minute conversation that ends in a

00:01:16.301 --> 00:01:16.896
decision?

00:01:16.896 --> 00:01:18.680
At the end, you'll show us.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:19.870
Let's get started.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:22.507
The course runs in five stages.

00:01:22.507 --> 00:01:27.617
First, the foundations: the framework
itself, then the ecosystem of tools.

00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:29.964
That's about two and a half hours.

00:01:29.964 --> 00:01:31.621
Next, you run the tools.

00:01:31.621 --> 00:01:36.386
There's one module each for the
Culture Mosaic, the Progress Monitor,

00:01:36.386 --> 00:01:40.321
the Leadership Mosaic 360,
Mosaic Signal and Culture Dig,

00:01:40.321 --> 00:01:42.738
and you can take them in any order.

00:01:42.738 --> 00:01:47.986
Then you learn to make sense of the
data, then to say it well to executives.

00:01:47.986 --> 00:01:51.921
Finally, the capstone, where
you show us what you can do.

00:01:51.921 --> 00:01:55.857
Plan on three to five weeks
at four to five hours a week.

00:01:55.857 --> 00:02:01.588
You have ninety days from enrollment, and
you can ask for one thirty-day extension.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.200
You're certified when
you clear four gates.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.939
Each one measures something different.

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:09.885
Gate one is module mastery.

00:02:09.885 --> 00:02:14.139
You pass each module check,
from Module 1 through Module 8,

00:02:14.139 --> 00:02:16.301
with eighty percent or higher.

00:02:16.301 --> 00:02:22.140
You also complete the setup simulations
for the Culture Mosaic and the Leadership

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.664
Mosaic 360 with no critical errors.

00:02:24.664 --> 00:02:29.782
A critical error is a mistake that
would hurt a client or a respondent,

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.016
such as exposing a small group.

00:02:32.016 --> 00:02:35.044
You can retake these as often as you like.

00:02:35.044 --> 00:02:40.955
Gate two is the final knowledge exam: fifty
questions across framework, ecosystem,

00:02:40.955 --> 00:02:43.911
setup and operations, and interpretation.

00:02:43.911 --> 00:02:46.867
It's seventy-five minutes and open notes.

00:02:46.867 --> 00:02:52.706
To pass, you need eighty percent overall,
at least seventy percent in every area,

00:02:52.706 --> 00:02:55.013
and every critical item correct.

00:02:55.013 --> 00:03:00.707
Critical items cover the few things a
Mosaic practitioner must never get wrong,

00:03:00.707 --> 00:03:05.033
like protecting anonymity and
not overclaiming the research.

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:10.800
Gate three is an interpretation memo on
the Northwind Health case: three to five

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:16.495
findings, the evidence for each, how
confident you are, and what you'd do next.

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:22.118
Gate four is a recorded ten to twelve
minute briefing to Northwind's executive

00:03:22.118 --> 00:03:25.506
team, plus short answers
to pushback questions.

00:03:25.506 --> 00:03:25.722
Dr.

00:03:25.722 --> 00:03:31.345
Chris Cancialosi scores both, and you
need at least three out of four on every

00:03:31.345 --> 00:03:32.066
criterion.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:36.131
When you pass, you're a
Certified Mosaic Practitioner.

00:03:36.131 --> 00:03:41.345
If you're a Mosaic partner, the certification
appears on your badge wall in the

00:03:41.345 --> 00:03:44.776
partner portal and earns
the Mosaic Certified badge.

00:03:44.776 --> 00:03:49.990
Each certification has a private verification
link you can share with a client.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:54.940
It shows your name, the certification,
its dates, and whether it's current.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:57.250
The certification lasts five years.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:02.662
Because the tools change, we may also ask
you to complete a short "What's changed"

00:04:02.662 --> 00:04:07.414
update when a major product change
affects something you were tested on.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.880
You'll learn faster by doing.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:15.480
The Mosaic Practice Workspace has ready-made
examples: a closed Culture Mosaic you

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:21.080
can generate a report from, and a Leadership
Mosaic 360 with seven raters plus the

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.788
leader's self-assessment.

00:04:22.788 --> 00:04:26.066
You can also build and
preview your own surveys.

00:04:26.066 --> 00:04:29.275
Test responses never show
in charts or reports,

00:04:29.275 --> 00:04:32.280
so practise reading
results on the examples.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.695
Every learner shares it,
so use made-up data only.

00:04:35.695 --> 00:04:40.134
It never sends email, and it's
wiped on the first of every month,

00:04:40.134 --> 00:04:42.251
so keep nothing there you need.

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:46.151
Throughout the course you'll
work with one client,

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:49.332
and in the capstone you'll
hold the whole file.

00:04:49.332 --> 00:04:54.002
Northwind Health is a regional health
system: one community hospital,

00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:58.063
six outpatient clinics, and six
hundred and forty employees.

00:04:58.063 --> 00:05:01.921
Eighteen months ago it merged
with Lakeside Clinic Group,

00:05:01.921 --> 00:05:04.696
which brought in four of the six clinics.

00:05:04.696 --> 00:05:07.336
The strategy is called "One Northwind".

00:05:07.336 --> 00:05:08.960
Three things worry them.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:13.630
Nursing turnover has climbed to
twenty-four percent, up from sixteen.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:17.285
Clinic staff say they "feel
like a different company".

00:05:17.285 --> 00:05:22.226
And leaders say the strategy is clear,
while the frontline says it isn't.

00:05:22.226 --> 00:05:25.881
Your sponsor is Alex Moreau,
the Chief People Officer.

00:05:25.881 --> 00:05:31.228
Alex wants to understand what the culture
actually looks like after the merger,

00:05:31.228 --> 00:05:34.545
help the senior team lead
the integration better,

00:05:34.545 --> 00:05:38.132
and show the board whether
anything moves the needle.

00:05:38.132 --> 00:05:43.005
Northwind is fictional, and every
figure in it was written for teaching.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.879
Every certified practitioner
signs on to a Code of Practice.

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:50.069
Here are its eight principles.

00:05:50.069 --> 00:05:52.770
One: protect the people who answered.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.397
Never try to work out who said what,

00:05:55.397 --> 00:05:59.923
and never show results for a
group below the report's minimum.

00:05:59.923 --> 00:06:04.375
When a client asks "who said
that?", the answer is always no.

00:06:04.375 --> 00:06:08.317
Two: tell respondents the
truth about confidentiality.

00:06:08.317 --> 00:06:13.280
In a Leadership Mosaic 360, boss
feedback is attributed to the boss,

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.397
and you say so before launch.

00:06:15.397 --> 00:06:18.681
Three: claim only what
the evidence supports.

00:06:18.681 --> 00:06:24.301
The research linking culture to performance
comes from comparable frameworks.

00:06:24.301 --> 00:06:29.119
It isn't Mosaic-specific validation,
and you describe it that way.

00:06:29.119 --> 00:06:33.425
A pattern is a hypothesis for
dialogue, not proof of cause.

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:36.929
Four: keep development
separate from evaluation.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:41.235
A 360 is for development, never
pay or promotion decisions.

00:06:41.235 --> 00:06:47.366
Five: respect data rights, including a
client's choice to stay out of the benchmark.

00:06:47.366 --> 00:06:49.629
Six: use the tools as designed.

00:06:49.629 --> 00:06:53.716
Don't alter locked items,
don't copy a purchased survey,

00:06:53.716 --> 00:06:57.001
and don't share a partner
code with a client.

00:06:57.001 --> 00:07:00.139
Seven: describe culture
without judging it.

00:07:00.139 --> 00:07:06.052
And eight: close the loop, by encouraging
every client to share what they learned

00:07:06.052 --> 00:07:08.241
with the people who took part.

00:07:08.733 --> 00:07:13.166
Before you start Module 1, read the
Code once more, then confirm it.

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:18.577
And if you like, jot down one sentence:
which principle do you expect to be hardest

00:07:18.577 --> 00:07:20.989
to hold to when a client pushes back?

00:07:20.989 --> 00:07:23.205
We'll come back to it in Module 9.

